%% ============================================
%% FRONTISPIECE — "全書一句話" spread built on the cycle's own key verse
%% (2:18-19), the same role Job 42:5-6, Acts 1:8 and Isaiah 12:2-3 play in
%% the sister volumes. The three-part division in the table below is
%% G. Campbell Morgan's own (The Analyzed Bible, 1907): Conditions after
%% Joshua (1:1-3:6), the Period of the Judges (3:7-16), Appendix (17-21).
%% ============================================
\thispagestyle{empty}
\begin{center}
\vspace*{0.3in}

\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[ScriptureGold, line width=0.8pt] (-2.8,0) -- (-0.55,0);
  \fill[ScriptureGold] (0,0) circle (0.055);
  \draw[ScriptureGold, line width=0.8pt] (0.55,0) -- (2.8,0);
\end{tikzpicture}

\vspace{0.22cm}
{\Large\bfseries\color{ChapterIron} 全書一句話 \textperiodcentered\ The Whole Book in One Verse}

\vspace{0.30cm}
\fcolorbox{ScriptureGold}{ScriptureBg}{%
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\centering\vspace{0.2cm}
\normalsize\color{CommentaryBrown}
耶和華為他們興起士師，就與那士師\textbf{\color{TorchOrange!80!black}同在}。……
及至士師死後，他們就轉去行惡，比他們列祖\textbf{\color{TorchOrange!80!black}更甚}。\\[0.5em]
\footnotesize\itshape
When the LORD raised up judges for them, the LORD was \textbf{with} the judge …\\
but it came about when the judge died, that they would turn back and act
\textbf{more corruptly} than their fathers.\\[0.4em]
\small\color{ChapterIron} 士師記 2:18-19 \textperiodcentered\ Judges 2:18-19
\vspace{0.2cm}
\end{minipage}}

\vspace{0.35cm}
{\small\color{TextGray} 二十一章 \textperiodcentered\ 九卷 \textperiodcentered\ 一圈一圈往下墮落的循環\\
\textit{Twenty-one chapters \textperiodcentered\ nine volumes \textperiodcentered\ a cycle that spirals downward, not in place}}

\vspace{0.30cm}
{\small
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.3}
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{2.8cm}p{2.4cm}p{6.9cm}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{段落} & \textbf{章節} & \textbf{在全書的展開} \\
\midrule
約書亞之後的光景 & 1-2章 & 未趕盡的迦南人，波金使者的責備，循環公式本身的交代——全書的引擎在此先講一遍 \\
士師循環 · 七次沉淪 & 3-16章 & 俄陀聶、以笏、底波拉、基甸、耶弗他、參孫等——一次比一次更深，士師本身也一次比一次更有瑕疵 \\
沒有王的亂象 & 17-21章 & 米迦的偶像、利未人之妾、便雅憫幾乎滅族——沒有外敵時，內部的爛透原形畢露 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
}

\vspace{0.4cm}
\textcolor{ScriptureGold}{\rule{2.5in}{0.7pt}}
\vspace{0.3cm}

{\bfseries\color{ChapterIron} 讀經之鑰 \textperiodcentered\ How to Read This Book}

\vspace{0.18cm}
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\small\color{TextGray}
不是來讀一本「屬靈英雄傳」，是來看一圈一圈收緊、卻始終沒有止住的墮落——
連神所興起的拯救者，也一個比一個更帶著破口。\\
若你讀完二十一章卻只記得「參孫很強壯」——請從頭再讀，\\
這次留意：每一位士師都救一時、救一地，沒有一位是完全的拯救者；
這卷書的空缺，正是留給你去問：誰才是那位真正的王？\\[0.5em]
\textit{\footnotesize
You are not reading a book of spiritual heroes — you are watching a downward
spiral that tightens circle by circle and never resolves on its own, where
even the deliverers God raises up carry one flaw after another.\\
If after twenty-one chapters you remember only "Samson was strong," read it again.\\
This time notice: not one judge is a complete deliverer — the book's own
unfinished ending asks you who the true King is.}
\end{minipage}

\vfill
{\scriptsize\color{LightGray} PubHub 三書精讀系統 \textperiodcentered\ Soli Deo Gloria}

